{
  "title": "Serious Eats combined flour ingredient drops filling quantity",
  "description": "The Serious Eats Croquetas de Jamon snapshot loses the flour \
quantity needed for the filling because it appears to trust the page's JSON-LD \
over the visible structured ingredient row.\n\
\n\
Concrete example:\n\
- Snapshot: \
data/pipeline-snapshots/seriouseats-com_croquetas-de-jamon-recipe-11680423.json\n\
- Cached HTML: \
~/.ramekin/http-cache/seriouseats-com_croquetas-de-jamon-recipe-11680423/response.bin\n\
- Visible HTML ingredient row: `1/2 cup plus 2 tablespoons all-purpose flour \
(80 g), plus 1 cup all-purpose flour (for dredging), divided`\n\
- JSON-LD ingredient row: `1 cup all-purpose flour, for dredging`\n\
- Snapshot produced only: `1 cup all-purpose flour, for dredging`\n\
\n\
The method later says to stir in `1/2 cup plus 2 tablespoons (80g) flour`, so \
a user relying on the ingredient list would miss the filling flour. Prefer the \
visible structured ingredient data when JSON-LD is less complete, or otherwise \
merge the missing quantity from the visible row.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pipeline",
    "ingredient-parser",
    "seriouseats",
  ],
